WEBVTT

00:00.000 --> 00:03.580
Do you think other people think that you're the Messiah?

00:04.860 --> 00:07.700
I came out of a conference speaking, and when I walked out the door,

00:07.800 --> 00:11.080
this mad lady comes running up to me and tries to kidnap me.

00:11.240 --> 00:11.540
What?

00:11.860 --> 00:12.160
Yeah.

00:14.240 --> 00:19.780
My job is to share a truth that everyone's been told is not real.

00:23.350 --> 00:28.270
It was 19 years ago, on January the 8th of 2007.

00:28.530 --> 00:31.330
I was down and out and lost everything.

00:31.330 --> 00:36.210
Lost my home, and I'm having to apply for free lunch for my kids.

00:36.430 --> 00:38.050
Sick with Crohn's disease.

00:38.390 --> 00:41.190
And if anybody has Crohn's, knows how bad that is.

00:41.290 --> 00:43.510
You know, you're in the restroom 10 times a day.

00:43.570 --> 00:45.870
I was it 20 times a day at that point.

00:46.880 --> 00:51.760
In January of 2007, while fishing with friends in North Carolina,

00:52.400 --> 00:57.640
Chris Bledsoe witnessed a series of bright, intelligently moving orbs in the sky.

00:58.140 --> 00:59.560
That moment doesn't end.

00:59.560 --> 01:02.080
It starts a series of unexpected,

01:02.400 --> 01:04.460
and seemingly miraculous events.

01:05.360 --> 01:07.600
And then my Crohn's was gone.

01:07.800 --> 01:08.900
I had no more sickness.

01:09.380 --> 01:12.780
In the days and weeks that follow, the phenomena continue.

01:13.440 --> 01:15.540
The lights appear again and again,

01:15.880 --> 01:17.260
sometimes at a distance,

01:17.660 --> 01:19.780
sometimes directly over his home.

01:20.240 --> 01:26.120
He reports numerous encounters that don't resemble crafts, lights, or UFOs at all.

01:26.120 --> 01:30.040
But what he describes as a luminous, feminine presence,

01:30.340 --> 01:32.120
deeply unsettling in its art,

01:32.320 --> 01:35.280
is an archetypal familiarity.

01:35.280 --> 01:41.620
Her communication seems to go beyond the cliches and platitudes of normal contact experiences.

01:41.620 --> 01:45.100
They touch on humanity's deep moral decay.

01:45.100 --> 01:50.980
Cycles of civilizational collapse, judgment, the apocalypse, and renewal.

01:50.980 --> 01:54.200
They revolve around humanity reaching a threshold.

01:54.200 --> 01:58.400
I came back excited to tell it.

01:58.400 --> 02:02.720
That's when the next five years of darkness, I talk about in my book,

02:02.720 --> 02:03.560
started.

02:04.160 --> 02:08.790
His UFO experiences only serve to make him more of a pariah

02:08.790 --> 02:11.790
in his local community of Fayetteville, North Carolina,

02:12.290 --> 02:15.510
where fundamentalist Christianity is the only way,

02:15.890 --> 02:18.530
and anything paranormal is considered demonic.

02:19.990 --> 02:23.190
NASA and the CIA show up at Bledsoe's door.

02:23.670 --> 02:26.250
And not just anybody at NASA and the CIA.

02:26.970 --> 02:30.210
I'm talking about a high-level NASA mission controller

02:30.210 --> 02:32.910
who has worked on launches at Cape Canaveral

02:32.910 --> 02:33.370
since the 2000s.

02:33.390 --> 02:35.310
Challenger missions in the 80s.

02:35.310 --> 02:38.350
And he said, I was at the dinner table with the president

02:38.350 --> 02:39.510
and handed me that.

02:39.510 --> 02:40.270
He said that?

02:40.270 --> 02:40.770
Yeah.

02:40.770 --> 02:41.270
Whoa.

02:41.270 --> 02:42.510
And this, yeah.

02:42.510 --> 02:45.990
Scientists, military, and other intelligence officials

02:45.990 --> 02:46.890
follow suit.

02:46.890 --> 02:49.530
They grill Bledsoe on his experiences.

02:49.530 --> 02:53.850
Some imply that certain dates and symbols he's given by the lady

02:53.850 --> 02:56.490
align with things they're already monitoring

02:56.490 --> 02:59.330
and have seen from other authoritative sources.

02:59.330 --> 03:02.830
So they have like a scientific model of how these angels,

03:02.830 --> 03:05.270
angels work at NASA.

03:05.270 --> 03:09.340
They know a lot more than we know than we think they do.

03:09.340 --> 03:12.700
I personally don't know what Chris Bledsoe experienced

03:12.700 --> 03:15.340
and continues to experience to this day.

03:15.340 --> 03:17.500
But I know that his story doesn't sit

03:17.500 --> 03:19.340
at the edge of history forever.

03:19.340 --> 03:22.140
It's either going to collapse under scrutiny

03:22.140 --> 03:24.280
or force us to redraw the map.

03:25.400 --> 03:27.820
In this special episode of American Alchemy,

03:27.820 --> 03:30.260
we have a markedly different conversation

03:30.260 --> 03:32.800
than the one that Chris Bledsoe is used to having.

03:32.800 --> 03:35.980
He took you to Zanesville, Ohio, where you recovered

03:35.980 --> 03:37.280
a little piece of metal?

03:37.280 --> 03:37.780
Yeah.

03:37.780 --> 03:39.580
Do you know who's from Zanesville, Ohio?

03:39.580 --> 03:40.180
Yeah, I do.

03:40.180 --> 03:41.620
T. Townsend Brown, right?

03:41.620 --> 03:43.430
What?

03:43.430 --> 03:45.710
Instead of just retelling his story,

03:45.710 --> 03:48.470
we make some pretty mind-blowing connections from it.

03:48.470 --> 03:52.350
Ones involving secret societies with access to time travel,

03:52.350 --> 03:55.790
anti-gravity experiments done in mid-century America,

03:55.790 --> 03:58.690
space metal with curious properties that interact

03:58.690 --> 04:01.170
with consciousness in weird ways.

04:01.170 --> 04:03.330
What exists on the dark side of the moon?

04:03.410 --> 04:07.640
And what the world will look like in the next decade?

04:07.640 --> 04:09.980
So without further ado, sit back, relax,

04:09.980 --> 04:12.540
and prepare to ascend into the astral plane

04:12.540 --> 04:19.990
with this week's American Alchemist, Christopher Bledsoe.

04:19.990 --> 04:22.090
This has been a long time coming.

04:22.090 --> 04:24.470
I'm here with Chris Bledsoe,

04:24.470 --> 04:27.870
who many call kind of a super-experiencer

04:27.870 --> 04:32.010
because I was just rereading your book, UFO of God,

04:32.010 --> 04:35.030
and your life is really just remarkable.

04:35.030 --> 04:36.750
You've had all these incredible, deep experiences,

04:36.750 --> 04:40.570
and I want to talk about those experiences.

04:40.570 --> 04:41.750
But I also want to talk,

04:41.750 --> 04:44.710
because your story is well-known at this point.

04:44.710 --> 04:48.730
I also want to talk about some of the deeper philosophies

04:48.730 --> 04:52.370
that you've kind of come into based on your experiences

04:52.370 --> 04:55.250
and maybe have kind of a metaphysical conversation.

04:55.250 --> 04:58.670
But I want to start with this very interesting discussion

04:58.670 --> 05:01.510
that we just kind of sparked up as you were walking in,

05:01.510 --> 05:04.610
which is you have this golden pin on your jacket.

05:04.610 --> 05:06.030
What is that pin?

05:06.030 --> 05:06.970
Well,

05:06.970 --> 05:10.370
that pin was given me

05:10.370 --> 05:14.570
by someone everybody has read about, right?

05:14.570 --> 05:17.910
Down at Cape Canaveral, without saying names.

05:17.910 --> 05:18.750
Okay.

05:18.750 --> 05:24.380
And it signifies being off-planet.

05:24.380 --> 05:25.940
So from what I'm told,

05:25.940 --> 05:29.660
the people that get these have been in space before.

05:29.660 --> 05:31.960
So astronauts, pretty much.

05:31.960 --> 05:32.840
Right, right.

05:32.840 --> 05:36.840
And why do you think this person gave that pin to you?

05:36.840 --> 05:37.940
At the time, I had no clue.

05:37.940 --> 05:40.940
I had no clue other than what they were telling me.

05:40.940 --> 05:45.440
It involved taking me into the astronaut crew quarters

05:45.440 --> 05:47.360
and going through a whole thing,

05:47.360 --> 05:50.950
because I was, in other words,

05:50.950 --> 05:53.050
when this thing first happened,

05:55.090 --> 05:58.670
this person from NASA came to my house with a backpack

05:58.670 --> 06:00.810
and a whole lot of credentials

06:00.810 --> 06:04.850
that had everything from Area 51 to the CIA

06:04.850 --> 06:08.100
and all that combined, NASA.

06:08.100 --> 06:10.200
And he tested the whole thing,

06:10.200 --> 06:12.860
tested the whole family with metal.

06:12.860 --> 06:14.460
He put a piece of metal in my hand.

06:14.460 --> 06:16.940
I was the last one to be tested.

06:16.940 --> 06:20.020
So all my, four of my kids and my wife,

06:20.020 --> 06:22.140
they all went into this one room.

06:22.140 --> 06:23.420
So she got Ryan.

06:23.420 --> 06:27.560
He got Ryan as the first one and kind of made it secret.

06:27.560 --> 06:30.420
He took Ryan into a room, tested him,

06:30.420 --> 06:33.580
and said, now you go get the next person, but don't tell them.

06:33.580 --> 06:37.020
So he went out and got each person in the family,

06:37.020 --> 06:39.890
tested them with this metal.

06:39.890 --> 06:40.910
They brought me in last.

06:40.910 --> 06:43.370
And I had no idea what I was doing.

06:43.370 --> 06:45.050
I sat down on the edge of the bed.

06:45.050 --> 06:47.880
It was in Ryan's room.

06:47.880 --> 06:49.680
And he put this piece of metal right here.

06:49.680 --> 06:51.760
And I said, what do you think of that?

06:51.760 --> 06:54.480
I said, well, it looks like a piece of aluminum,

06:54.480 --> 06:56.020
like a postage stamp.

06:56.020 --> 06:57.700
Size, that size, thin.

06:59.640 --> 07:00.480
Was it light?

07:00.480 --> 07:01.720
Very light, yeah.

07:01.720 --> 07:03.220
It was kind of a dull gray.

07:03.220 --> 07:04.540
It wasn't like shiny.

07:04.540 --> 07:07.220
It was aluminum of some sort.

07:07.220 --> 07:09.180
And he reaches in his backpack

07:09.180 --> 07:12.120
and pulls out another piece of metal that was different.

07:12.420 --> 07:14.460
And it was like aluminum foil.

07:14.460 --> 07:16.360
Looked like foil.

07:16.360 --> 07:17.420
And it wasn't creased.

07:17.420 --> 07:20.020
You couldn't crease it, but it would wrinkle,

07:20.020 --> 07:22.360
but it would hold back out.

07:22.360 --> 07:23.440
But it wouldn't crease.

07:23.440 --> 07:24.340
You couldn't crease it.

07:24.340 --> 07:27.660
You could, it would kind of roll up and then straighten out.

07:27.660 --> 07:30.580
But when he put that in this hand,

07:30.580 --> 07:33.680
it somehow or another created this current

07:33.680 --> 07:37.150
that went through where it was communicating.

07:37.150 --> 07:40.250
This part of the metal was communicating

07:40.250 --> 07:41.550
with that part of the metal.

07:41.550 --> 07:42.690
And when that happened,

07:43.630 --> 07:45.790
it caused me to, my eyes to roll back.

07:45.790 --> 07:48.570
And he reached up and snatched it out of my hand real quick

07:48.570 --> 07:49.810
and said, why you?

07:49.810 --> 07:52.740
This is in the book, by the way.

07:52.740 --> 07:54.580
And I had no idea what happened.

07:54.580 --> 07:57.820
He said, why you this close?

07:57.820 --> 08:00.740
I said, excuse me, what do you mean, what I mean?

08:00.740 --> 08:04.420
He said, well, I would have known you were lying

08:04.420 --> 08:09.420
about being taken if you hadn't had a reaction to this.

08:10.860 --> 08:13.180
And he said, I've only ever seen two others

08:13.180 --> 08:14.860
and they were nothing like yours.

08:15.260 --> 08:17.380
That's what he told me.

08:17.380 --> 08:22.820
So that started the next two, three years studying with them.

08:27.720 --> 08:31.180
And I'm being kind to my friend without saying his name,

08:31.180 --> 08:32.520
but you know who I'm talking about.

08:32.520 --> 08:33.820
I know who you're talking about.

08:33.820 --> 08:35.060
Can I say who it is?

08:35.060 --> 08:37.160
Because it's, I think it's Tim Taylor,

08:37.160 --> 08:39.420
who's a NASA mission controller,

08:39.420 --> 08:42.500
who, yeah, his name is now sort of out there.

08:42.500 --> 08:45.660
And yeah, we should definitely be respectful to him

08:45.660 --> 08:46.400
as somebody who doesn't.

08:46.400 --> 08:49.400
Maybe want to do public interviews himself,

08:49.400 --> 08:53.830
but I think he's put himself out there enough to, you know.

08:53.830 --> 08:56.270
So who is this Timothy Taylor figure

08:56.270 --> 08:58.370
showing up in Bledsoe's life?

08:58.370 --> 09:00.610
He's a mysterious rocket scientist

09:00.610 --> 09:03.610
who's done mission control for NASA since the 80s.

09:03.610 --> 09:05.550
That part is not really disputed

09:05.550 --> 09:08.050
and it's well-documented in his autobiography,

09:08.050 --> 09:09.150
Launch Fever.

09:09.150 --> 09:12.390
At one point, Tim Taylor even had a small YouTube account

09:12.390 --> 09:15.030
with videos showing his deep levels of access

09:15.030 --> 09:16.450
to NASA facilities.

09:16.450 --> 09:18.450
He's also taken people like Bledsoe

09:18.450 --> 09:20.130
through Kennedy Space Center.

09:20.130 --> 09:22.530
Religious studies professor Diana Pasolka,

09:22.530 --> 09:25.330
along with others, have said that he's worked directly

09:25.330 --> 09:26.970
with Elon Musk.

09:26.970 --> 09:29.890
But where it gets interesting is that he's also popping up

09:29.890 --> 09:32.770
in the lives of numerous UFO experiencers,

09:32.770 --> 09:37.710
claiming that he's a time traveler and works for an angel.

09:37.710 --> 09:40.170
Basically, he exists at the intersection

09:40.170 --> 09:43.310
between rigorous real-world aerospace work

09:43.310 --> 09:45.710
and totally insane UFO lore.

09:45.710 --> 09:47.190
And that's why he's still amazing.

09:47.190 --> 09:51.760
He's one of American Alchemy's most requested guests.

09:51.760 --> 09:54.540
Some of the things that Tim Taylor told Chris

09:54.540 --> 09:58.400
would wholesale overhaul our understanding of reality,

09:58.400 --> 09:59.780
if at all true.

09:59.780 --> 10:04.530
Really smart guy, like genius level, and, uh.

10:04.530 --> 10:05.370
Really?

10:05.370 --> 10:06.210
Yeah.

10:06.210 --> 10:07.570
I enjoyed his company.

10:07.570 --> 10:09.210
We did a lot of stuff together.

10:09.210 --> 10:10.750
We traveled together.

10:10.750 --> 10:16.080
Um, we were able to recover some metal together.

10:16.080 --> 10:17.060
Wow.

10:17.060 --> 10:17.880
Yeah.

10:17.880 --> 10:18.720
I didn't know that.

10:18.720 --> 10:19.560
Yeah.

10:19.560 --> 10:20.900
I was in Ohio.

10:20.900 --> 10:21.860
In Ohio?

10:21.860 --> 10:22.700
Yeah.

10:22.700 --> 10:23.740
Where in Ohio?

10:23.740 --> 10:26.340
In a little town called Zanes, well.

10:26.340 --> 10:27.160
Zanesville.

10:27.160 --> 10:28.000
Zanesville, yeah.

10:28.000 --> 10:29.400
Zanesville, Ohio.

10:29.400 --> 10:30.240
Yeah.

10:30.240 --> 10:31.480
Do you know who's from Zanesville, Ohio?

10:31.480 --> 10:32.400
Yeah, I do.

10:32.400 --> 10:33.840
T-town's in Brown, right?

