11:17.060 --> 11:18.760
No way.

11:18.760 --> 11:22.720
And when he found out about me and read the story,

11:22.720 --> 11:23.960
he calls me and says,

11:23.960 --> 11:25.560
I got something I want you to see.

11:25.560 --> 11:29.000
And so I called Taylor and he and I flew up there.

11:32.000 --> 11:37.040
This is either engineered to make me excited

11:37.040 --> 11:41.460
or this is the most remarkable story ever.

11:41.460 --> 11:48.300
I almost lost it during this part of the interview.

11:48.300 --> 11:51.180
Zanesville, Ohio, is where Thomas Townsend Brown

11:51.180 --> 11:52.220
was born.

11:52.220 --> 11:54.860
To me, Townsend Brown is the most interesting

11:54.860 --> 11:56.920
historical figure in the 20th century

11:56.920 --> 11:58.560
that no one knows about.

11:58.560 --> 12:01.860
I've independently uncovered an absurd amount of information

12:01.860 --> 12:04.160
that leads me to believe that Townsend Brown

12:04.160 --> 12:08.490
essentially discovered anti-gravity in the 1950s.

12:08.490 --> 12:10.990
He was funded by the same physics patrons

12:10.990 --> 12:13.690
