experience it and then other people walk away

02:58:59.690 --> 02:59:01.470
and they're like, yeah, I don't know, it was a thing,

02:59:01.470 --> 02:59:04.130
it happened or whatever, or they like,

02:59:04.130 --> 02:59:08.150
we'll superimpose some prosaic explanation upon the thing.

02:59:08.150 --> 02:59:11.890
And reality itself is far more fractured, malleable,

02:59:11.890 --> 02:59:14.770
and in the eye of the beholder than what it is.

02:59:14.770 --> 02:59:16.010
Yeah, and it's changing.

02:59:16.010 --> 02:59:18.810
It's constantly changing like the Mandela effect

02:59:18.810 --> 02:59:19.830
you talked about.

02:59:19.830 --> 02:59:23.200
One thing that surprised me is my wife

02:59:23.200 --> 02:59:26.240
and I've been married 43 years, right?

02:59:26.240 --> 02:59:28.860
So our honeymoon was in New York City.

02:59:28.860 --> 02:59:31.260
We'd never been there, either one of us.

02:59:31.820 --> 02:59:32.860
We had a plan.

02:59:32.860 --> 02:59:35.300
We wanted to see the train station,

02:59:35.300 --> 02:59:37.280
Grand Central Station, right?

02:59:37.280 --> 02:59:39.000
So we go to Grand Central Station

02:59:39.000 --> 02:59:42.100
and we get photos and videos and we took a helicopter ride

02:59:42.100 --> 02:59:45.180
and we did all kind of things to experience New York.

02:59:46.550 --> 02:59:49.030
And so I'm looking at my old photos

02:59:49.030 --> 02:59:52.080
of Grand Central Station, right?

02:59:52.080 --> 02:59:53.900
Well, Google it now.

02:59:53.900 --> 02:59:56.600
It's not called that, it's called Grand Central Terminal

02:59:56.600 --> 02:59:59.380
and it says it's never been called that.

02:59:59.380 --> 03:00:02.000
But yet I got photos of Grand Central Station.

03:00:02.000 --> 03:00:02.840
Yeah.

03:00:02.840 --> 03:00:03.660
Written on the thing.

03:00:03.660 --> 03:00:04.500
Yeah, yeah, yeah, yeah.

03:00:04.500 --> 03:00:07.420
But you see it now, it says Grand Central Terminal.

03:00:07.420 --> 03:00:09.260
What's that about?

03:00:09.260 --> 03:00:12.420
Well, you know, the Flintstones,

03:00:12.420 --> 03:00:15.480
the Berenstys, Berenstein Bears,

03:00:15.480 --> 03:00:18.820
all these things where people swear

03:00:18.820 --> 03:00:20.880
that, you know, it was like one way

03:00:20.880 --> 03:00:22.600
and then you look at the record

03:00:22.600 --> 03:00:24.520
and it actually looks like there's another way.

03:00:24.520 --> 03:00:25.360
Yeah.

03:00:25.360 --> 03:00:29.280
And, you know, it is this really amazing phenomena.

03:00:29.280 --> 03:00:30.920
And then you get into deeper studies,

03:00:30.920 --> 03:00:32.000
like there's this neuroscience.

03:00:32.000 --> 03:00:34.340
I mean, you know, there's a scientist, Wilder Penfield,

03:00:34.340 --> 03:00:38.380
and you realize that there is no way of distinguishing

03:00:38.380 --> 03:00:40.780
between false memories and true memories.

03:00:40.780 --> 03:00:42.900
And he shows this with the ability

03:00:42.900 --> 03:00:45.340
to implant false memories into mice and stuff.

03:00:46.480 --> 03:00:48.800
And then you get, if there are these beings

03:00:48.800 --> 03:00:51.060
and any thoughts can be sort of implanted,

03:00:51.060 --> 03:00:53.480
you get into really weird ontological territory

03:00:53.480 --> 03:00:57.380
where the past, and even Schrodinger himself would say,

03:00:57.380 --> 03:00:59.200
a particle is measured in the present,

03:00:59.200 --> 03:01:01.840
you know, it might change its past.

03:01:01.840 --> 03:01:02.680
Right.

03:01:02.680 --> 03:01:05.240
And you get into retrocausality in quantum mechanics.

03:01:05.240 --> 03:01:07.440
There's obviously spooky action at a distance,

03:01:07.440 --> 03:01:09.720
but there's also spooky action across time.

03:01:09.720 --> 03:01:10.560
Right.

03:01:10.560 --> 03:01:15.040
It seems like if you have two entangled photons

03:01:15.040 --> 03:01:17.880
and two double slit experiments run with those,

03:01:17.880 --> 03:01:19.020
you know, entangled photons,

03:01:19.020 --> 03:01:21.180
seems like photon B that you're doing the experiment

03:01:21.180 --> 03:01:22.440
with two days in the future,

03:01:22.440 --> 03:01:24.720
if you measure that and you don't measure the first one,

03:01:24.720 --> 03:01:26.400
the measurement of the one in the future

03:01:26.400 --> 03:01:29.320
is affecting the one of the measurement in the past.

03:01:29.320 --> 03:01:30.160
Exactly.

03:01:30.160 --> 03:01:31.840
There's a great book called Biocentrism,

03:01:31.840 --> 03:01:34.580
that this guy Robert Lanza writes about this stuff.

03:01:34.580 --> 03:01:36.460
So you get into really trippy territory

03:01:36.460 --> 03:01:39.350
where the past becomes,

03:01:39.350 --> 03:01:41.990
the present is this constricted present,

03:01:41.990 --> 03:01:44.970
but it's like an hourglass where you have probable futures

03:01:44.970 --> 03:01:46.250
and probable pasts.

03:01:46.250 --> 03:01:47.090
Right.

03:01:47.090 --> 03:01:48.850
And the present is this measurement sensor

03:01:48.850 --> 03:01:52.030
that is single line of code updating the past

03:01:52.030 --> 03:01:54.310
and maybe updating the future at the same time.

03:01:54.310 --> 03:01:55.150
Right.

03:01:55.150 --> 03:01:57.510
And it's this very strange sort of model,

03:01:57.510 --> 03:02:01.350
but there's no real way to argue against that

03:02:01.350 --> 03:02:02.910
other than physical artifacts.

03:02:02.910 --> 03:02:05.590
So if you have physical artifacts around an event happening,

03:02:05.590 --> 03:02:07.170
you can argue, say this is evidence

03:02:07.170 --> 03:02:10.170
that this happened this way or this happened another way.

03:02:10.170 --> 03:02:12.230
If you have conflicting physical artifacts

03:02:12.230 --> 03:02:14.550
where you don't have physical artifacts,

03:02:14.550 --> 03:02:17.870
it's totally one word against the other word

03:02:17.870 --> 03:02:19.910
or you can get into like numbers of people

03:02:19.910 --> 03:02:20.950
who believe one thing

03:02:20.950 --> 03:02:22.630
or numbers of people that believe another thing.

03:02:22.630 --> 03:02:25.710
But we have no idea how reality works.

03:02:25.710 --> 03:02:27.130
We have no idea.

03:02:27.130 --> 03:02:31.130
We have a very limited, we are measurement sensors.

03:02:31.130 --> 03:02:34.270
And so this idea that science

03:02:34.270 --> 03:02:36.510
is some ontological statement of truth,

03:02:36.510 --> 03:02:39.350
like no, it's the map, it's not the territory.

03:02:39.350 --> 03:02:40.190
Exactly.

03:02:40.190 --> 03:02:43.950
It's just we see very limited scopes of reality.

03:02:43.950 --> 03:02:44.790
Right.

03:02:44.790 --> 03:02:46.450
And time is the weirdest thing of all.

03:02:46.450 --> 03:02:49.150
Yeah, that has messed with me

03:02:49.150 --> 03:02:51.530
ever since I went there and saw that.

03:02:51.530 --> 03:02:53.510
And now everything I dig up,

03:02:53.510 --> 03:02:55.370
it says it was never called that.

03:02:55.370 --> 03:02:56.830
Yeah, Grand Central, yeah.

03:02:56.830 --> 03:02:57.670
But the sign was on the wall.

03:02:57.670 --> 03:02:59.190
It's funny, as you said Grand Central Station,

03:02:59.190 --> 03:03:01.130
I was like, oh, of course, Grand Central Station.

03:03:01.130 --> 03:03:03.870
Go Google it now though, it's not that.

03:03:03.870 --> 03:03:06.510
Grand Central Terminal, it doesn't even sound as good.

03:03:06.510 --> 03:03:09.670
Yeah, it's always been named that according to this.

03:03:09.670 --> 03:03:10.670
Yeah.

03:03:10.670 --> 03:03:12.330
So I don't know what that means,

03:03:12.330 --> 03:03:16.260
but it was really, it really opened my eyes

03:03:16.260 --> 03:03:20.580
to how weird this world we live in really is.

03:03:20.580 --> 03:03:24.470
How do you juggle, you know,

03:03:24.470 --> 03:03:26.470
a lot of these concepts might seem crazy

03:03:26.470 --> 03:03:27.570
to the average person.

03:03:27.570 --> 03:03:31.860
How do you juggle just facing, you know,

03:03:32.020 --> 03:03:35.420
relationships, issues, things in your own life

03:03:35.420 --> 03:03:40.420
versus these kind of deeper celestial metaphysical truths?

03:03:40.420 --> 03:03:43.920
Those two things seem kind of hard to juggle.

03:03:43.920 --> 03:03:45.320
I was talking to a friend yesterday

03:03:45.320 --> 03:03:47.760
and he has all these teachers, you know,

03:03:47.760 --> 03:03:49.220
kind of in the Eastern tradition.

03:03:49.220 --> 03:03:51.960
He's kind of his own mystic in a sense.

03:03:51.960 --> 03:03:53.680
And I think I can say this actually,

03:03:53.680 --> 03:03:54.780
his name is Duncan Trussell.

03:03:54.780 --> 03:03:57.140
And he's, you know, I actually just met him.

03:03:57.140 --> 03:04:00.100
He's an amazing comedian, but I felt a kinship with him.

03:04:00.100 --> 03:04:01.600
And he talked, he said, he said, he said, I don't know,

03:04:01.600 --> 03:04:06.000
he said his teachers all said that,

03:04:06.000 --> 03:04:07.660
and these are like Eastern, you know,

03:04:07.660 --> 03:04:09.920
kind of Buddhists say that, you know,

03:04:09.920 --> 03:04:12.540
they know that the celestial realm exists,

03:04:12.540 --> 03:04:14.920
but they ignore it because what we need to do

03:04:14.920 --> 03:04:17.840
is here on earth, we have these kind of karmic path

03:04:17.840 --> 03:04:19.700
laid out in front of you.

03:04:19.700 --> 03:04:22.160
So I'm sure a lot of people have this sort of escapist

03:04:22.160 --> 03:04:24.700
orientation towards this subject where they say,

03:04:24.700 --> 03:04:27.540
oh, well, take me up on the craft, you know?

03:04:27.540 --> 03:04:29.740
So how do you reconcile those two things?

03:04:29.740 --> 03:04:36.180
I don't, I mean, it's like, it's just,

03:04:36.180 --> 03:04:37.860
it's mind-bending, the whole thing.

03:04:37.860 --> 03:04:42.870
I'm still grappling with that, you know, to this very day.

03:04:42.870 --> 03:04:48.860
And I focus on, right now, my main focus

03:04:49.460 --> 03:04:51.640
is on the Rosetta Stone.

03:04:51.640 --> 03:04:53.220
Really?

03:04:53.220 --> 03:04:55.640
Why is your focus on the Rosetta Stone?

03:04:55.640 --> 03:05:00.640
Because I believe that I can find, I think I can get there.

03:05:00.780 --> 03:05:02.920
I think, I know it's talking.

03:05:02.980 --> 03:05:03.820
I know it is.

03:05:03.820 --> 03:05:06.060
I know it's talking multiple ways,

03:05:07.010 --> 03:05:08.430
not just telepathically,

03:05:08.430 --> 03:05:11.390
because that's hard to prove or explain,

03:05:11.390 --> 03:05:15.900
but I'm sure it's talking through frequency,

03:05:15.900 --> 03:05:18.020
through the light, pulses of light,

03:05:19.960 --> 03:05:21.480
with the right sensors,

03:05:21.480 --> 03:05:25.180
and even some sort of Morse code or something.

03:05:25.180 --> 03:05:27.520
Multiple ways it's trying to communicate.

03:05:27.520 --> 03:05:29.180
I've seen it, I know it,

03:05:29.180 --> 03:05:31.580
and I think one day we'll get there.

03:05:31.580 --> 03:05:33.380
You think the Rosetta Stone is trying to communicate?

03:05:33.380 --> 03:05:38.380
I think the Phenomenon is trying to talk to us,

03:05:39.200 --> 03:05:43.400
and to find that Rosetta Stone, you know,

03:05:43.400 --> 03:05:46.420
that's just the language.

03:05:46.420 --> 03:05:48.220
I want to find the language of this.

03:05:48.220 --> 03:05:50.060
Of the beings.

03:05:50.060 --> 03:05:53.520
Yeah, and it's putting it out right now, it's talking.

03:05:53.520 --> 03:05:58.300
We just got to study it, and I'm working on a way to do that.

03:05:58.300 --> 03:06:01.460
Do you think their language is discoveries?

03:06:01.460 --> 03:06:03.480
Like the discoveries we make?

03:06:03.480 --> 03:06:04.320
Yeah.

03:06:04.320 --> 03:06:05.320
What do you think the language is?

03:06:05.320 --> 03:06:08.000
Do you think it's a literal symbols and hieroglyphics?

03:06:08.000 --> 03:06:10.220
Because people say on the crafts that, you know,

03:06:10.220 --> 03:06:11.940
they see these sort of hieroglyphics.

03:06:11.940 --> 03:06:12.760
Yeah.

03:06:12.760 --> 03:06:15.660
I've heard biblical texts and all on them too.

03:06:17.190 --> 03:06:19.350
And you think we'll be able to decode this?

03:06:19.350 --> 03:06:23.690
I think we can get actual real-time communication

03:06:23.690 --> 03:06:25.490
through the light and through sensors.

03:06:25.490 --> 03:06:27.730
If we can gather enough data.

03:06:28.760 --> 03:06:29.780
How would we do this?

03:06:29.780 --> 03:06:32.360
Put it in a quantum AI computer.

03:06:32.360 --> 03:06:33.200
Mm.

03:06:33.200 --> 03:06:38.100
And there's two of them that I could probably get access to.

03:06:38.100 --> 03:06:39.400
So you're working on this?

03:06:39.400 --> 03:06:40.460
I'm working on it, yeah.

03:06:40.460 --> 03:06:43.000
Have you decoded anything yet?

03:06:43.000 --> 03:06:44.460
Well, we're working on it.

03:06:44.460 --> 03:06:45.300
That's all I can say.

03:06:45.300 --> 03:06:47.220
Well, it sounds like you have decoded a little thing or two.

03:06:47.220 --> 03:06:48.760
Some, some, yeah.

03:06:48.760 --> 03:06:51.000
Anything you can give us?

03:06:51.000 --> 03:06:53.640
Enough to get me going full-time.

03:06:53.640 --> 03:06:56.320
I'm saying anything you can give us as far as,

03:06:56.320 --> 03:06:57.900
hints as to what you've decoded.

03:06:57.900 --> 03:07:00.500
Well, just that I know it's there.

03:07:00.500 --> 03:07:02.460
And I think we'll be able to do that.

03:07:02.460 --> 03:07:02.660
Yeah. And I think we'll be able to do that.

03:07:02.660 --> 03:07:02.680
And I think we'll be able to do that.

03:07:02.680 --> 03:07:03.720
And I think we'll get there

03:07:03.720 --> 03:07:05.820
in the next four or five years, maybe.

03:07:05.820 --> 03:07:07.340
Maybe longer.

03:07:07.340 --> 03:07:09.760
Do you think there's something special

03:07:09.760 --> 03:07:13.840
about the pyramids that we'll learn soon or something?

03:07:13.840 --> 03:07:15.420
Because, I mean, one of your experiences

03:07:15.420 --> 03:07:16.920
was around the pyramids.

03:07:16.920 --> 03:07:18.480
Obviously, Hathor, Egyptian goddess.

03:07:18.480 --> 03:07:21.680
Well, I'm hearing that next year

03:07:21.680 --> 03:07:26.460
that something might be revealed from there.

03:07:26.460 --> 03:07:28.160
What will it be?

03:07:28.160 --> 03:07:30.900
Well, without getting ahead of what I was told this week,

03:07:30.900 --> 03:07:32.800
I've been invited to go down there.

03:07:32.840 --> 03:07:35.620
And be involved in something

03:07:35.620 --> 03:07:41.580
that is going to release something that was hidden.

03:07:41.580 --> 03:07:42.460
Interesting.

03:07:42.460 --> 03:07:44.160
And what?

03:07:44.160 --> 03:07:45.660
Something under the pyramids?

03:07:45.660 --> 03:07:46.840
Possibly.

03:07:46.840 --> 03:07:49.180
Like a little energy grid thing?

03:07:49.180 --> 03:07:50.380
They didn't tell me that.

03:07:50.380 --> 03:07:51.220
Okay.

03:07:51.220 --> 03:07:52.680
They just invited me to be a part.

03:07:52.680 --> 03:07:57.320
And the Egyptian antiquities authorities are part of it.

03:07:57.320 --> 03:07:58.160
Fascinating.

03:07:58.160 --> 03:07:59.380
Well, I just interviewed the guy

03:07:59.380 --> 03:08:03.000
that did the synthetic aperture radar Doppler tomography scans.

03:08:03.000 --> 03:08:07.180
Of the structure under the Khafre chamber of the Giza pyramid.

03:08:07.180 --> 03:08:08.920
I can't say that's what it is.

03:08:08.920 --> 03:08:11.560
I can just say I got a call from the right people

03:08:11.560 --> 03:08:14.580
that wants me to be a part next year.

03:08:14.580 --> 03:08:15.560
Well, that's exciting.

03:08:15.560 --> 03:08:16.770
Yeah.

03:08:16.770 --> 03:08:17.610
Very interesting.

03:08:17.610 --> 03:08:19.450
So I think something's coming from there

03:08:19.450 --> 03:08:21.090
that's gonna be real interesting.

03:08:21.090 --> 03:08:22.110
Wow.

03:08:22.110 --> 03:08:25.850
Like changing, thought changing.

03:08:25.850 --> 03:08:26.690
Wow.

03:08:26.690 --> 03:08:27.530
Yeah.

03:08:27.530 --> 03:08:28.970
Danny Jones, it was funny.

03:08:28.970 --> 03:08:32.050
Danny Jones, I think, came into your interview with him,

03:08:32.050 --> 03:08:33.550
maybe a little skeptical, but then he said,

03:08:33.550 --> 03:08:36.670
he saw an orb with you outside of a diner or something.

03:08:36.670 --> 03:08:37.510
Well, he called me.

03:08:37.510 --> 03:08:38.970
He's like, I want you on my show.

03:08:38.970 --> 03:08:41.550
I'm like, Danny, I'd love to be on your show,

03:08:41.550 --> 03:08:44.670
but you gotta do something for me.

03:08:45.630 --> 03:08:48.020
I'm gonna come a day or two early

03:08:48.020 --> 03:08:50.900
and I'm gonna make you a believer, not a skeptic.

03:08:50.900 --> 03:08:52.820
Because our interview will go differently

03:08:52.820 --> 03:08:54.880
if you're a believer.

03:08:54.880 --> 03:08:56.000
And he said, okay, okay.

03:08:56.000 --> 03:09:00.180
So we flew down, my daughter and I and my wife,

03:09:00.180 --> 03:09:03.380
and we had dinner there in Clearwater.

03:09:03.380 --> 03:09:06.180
Went over to Indian Rocks Beach out on the beach

03:09:06.180 --> 03:09:08.640
and he had his assistant with him with a camera.

03:09:08.640 --> 03:09:12.100
And I said, well, let's watch out of the ocean

03:09:12.100 --> 03:09:16.000
because I can get it, it appears up out of the ocean

03:09:16.000 --> 03:09:16.840
when I ask it.

03:09:16.840 --> 03:09:19.940
It's just like out of the sky, it comes up out of the sea.

03:09:19.940 --> 03:09:22.900
And suddenly here it came, two of them.

03:09:22.900 --> 03:09:23.760
Wow.

03:09:23.760 --> 03:09:26.360
And he filmed it, we all filmed it.

03:09:26.360 --> 03:09:27.200
Was he freaking out?

03:09:27.200 --> 03:09:28.200
Yeah.

03:09:28.200 --> 03:09:29.040
Wow.

03:09:29.040 --> 03:09:30.040
Yeah.

03:09:30.040 --> 03:09:31.720
We did that last week in California.

03:09:31.720 --> 03:09:32.560
Yeah.

03:09:32.560 --> 03:09:33.400
Yeah.

03:09:33.400 --> 03:09:34.240
Yeah.

03:09:34.240 --> 03:09:35.500
With some pretty amazing people.

03:09:35.500 --> 03:09:36.440
Wow.

03:09:36.440 --> 03:09:38.280
He also, Danny said he,

03:09:38.280 --> 03:09:41.100
I think he cut a small part of your interview

03:09:41.100 --> 03:09:42.960
where you talked about a neuralyzer,

03:09:42.960 --> 03:09:46.300
like some like machine that erased your memory

03:09:46.300 --> 03:09:47.740
after seeing something.

03:09:47.740 --> 03:09:49.300
Yeah, I had to not talk about that.

03:09:49.300 --> 03:09:50.900
You're not supposed to talk about that.

03:09:50.900 --> 03:09:53.440
But there is something like that that you experienced?

03:09:53.440 --> 03:09:55.080
I saw the patterns on it.

03:09:55.080 --> 03:09:55.920
Really?

03:09:55.920 --> 03:09:56.790
Yeah.

03:09:56.790 --> 03:09:58.490
So, I mean, that's freaky if the government

03:09:58.490 --> 03:10:00.830
has something that can do that.

03:10:00.830 --> 03:10:03.190
Let's just say they can transmit chemicals

03:10:03.190 --> 03:10:04.530
through radio waves.

03:10:06.080 --> 03:10:07.640
Do you think they can transmit thoughts

03:10:07.640 --> 03:10:08.960
through radio waves?

03:10:08.960 --> 03:10:10.180
Yeah.

03:10:11.180 --> 03:10:12.000
That's kind of creepy.

03:10:12.000 --> 03:10:14.680
Well, then I get into all sorts of weird territory.

03:10:14.680 --> 03:10:18.680
Like what is the whole UFO phenomenon?

03:10:18.680 --> 03:10:22.440
Some paranormal plague from the thought transmission?

03:10:22.440 --> 03:10:25.760
